*private
*.private
*.private.*
# AI assistant settings and state. Never sync these: they carry permission
# rules, MCP server configs, per-project transcripts and memory. What is
# authored rather than accumulated is synced, and is named here: the
# hand-written skills under $HOME/.claude/skills/, the symlinks under
# $HOME/.cursor/skills/ that name them, so that both tools read one SKILL.md and
# a skill cannot drift between them, and $HOME/.claude/statusline.sh.
#
# Each directory is reopened before anything in it can be admitted, because
# nothing under an excluded directory can be re-included and both are excluded
# by the operator's global ignore as well as here. So the first line reopens the
# directory for git to descend into, the second closes it again, and what
# follows names what to keep. Everything unnamed stays ignored: settings.json,
# CLAUDE.md, the transcripts under projects/, Cursor's mcp.json and
# cli-config.json, and the skills Cursor vendors into skills-cursor/. A bundle
# dropped into skills/ itself would now be staged rather than ignored, but it
# arrives as untracked files that `git status` names before a commit can take
# them.
#
# `**/`: a pattern holding a slash anchors to this file's own directory, so a
# bare `.claude/settings.json` would look for one beside .gitignore and match
# nothing under root/.
!**/.claude/
**/.claude/*
!**/.claude/skills/
!**/.claude/statusline.sh
!**/.cursor/
**/.cursor/*
!**/.cursor/skills/
**/.claude.json
**/.config/claude-code/
**/.gemini/
**/.antigravity/
**/.config/Antigravity/
**/.continue/
**/.config/opencode/
**/.config/kilo/
# Unanchored, so one written anywhere in the tree is caught and not only the
# copy under root/$HOME. A session working from a fresh clone has no global
# ignore to fall back on.
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
GEMINI.md
# Editor state, which carries the text of a file and not only its name. `sops
# edit` decrypts into a tempfile and the editor writes an undo history for it,
# so a synced undo directory takes plaintext out of the store and into a public
# repository. The directory rather than the sops names: an undo file is named
# after the path it belongs to, and every file edited has one.
#
# `**/` because a pattern holding a slash anchors to this file's own directory,
# and the tree it has to match is under root/.
**/.vim/tmp/
# The same for what vim keeps between sessions. `.vim/tmp/` above is where this
# repo's vimrc puts it; this is the location every other vim uses, which a host
# with a different vimrc still writes.
**/.viminfo
# Unanchored for the reason the three above are: a sops file is named for what
# it holds wherever it lands, including a copy made outside root/$HOME.
*.sops.yml
*.sops.yaml
*.sops.json
